1. CSS Selectors
A selector is used to select HTML elements that we want to style.
A. Element Selector
Selects all elements of a particular type.
p {
    color: blue;
}
This applies to all <p> elements.
<p>Hello</p>
<p>Welcome</p>

B. ID Selector
Selects an element using its id.
<h1 id="title">Welcome</h1>
#title {
    color: red;
}
# is used for an ID selector.
An ID should generally be unique on a page.

C. Class Selector
Selects elements using a class.
<p class="text">Hello</p>
<p class="text">Welcome</p>
.text {
    color: green;
}
. is used for a class selector.

D. Universal Selector
Selects all HTML elements.
* {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
}

E. Group Selector
Used when multiple elements have the same styling.
h1, h2, p {
    color: blue;
}

2. CSS Box Model
Every HTML element is treated as a box.
The CSS Box Model consists of:
┌───────────────────────────────┐
│            Margin             │
│  ┌─────────────────────────┐  │
│  │         Border          │  │
│  │  ┌───────────────────┐  │  │
│  │  │      Padding      │  │  │
│  │  │  ┌─────────────┐  │  │  │
│  │  │  │   Content   │  │  │  │
│  │  │  └─────────────┘  │  │  │
│  │  └───────────────────┘  │  │
│  └─────────────────────────┘  │
└───────────────────────────────┘
The four parts are:
Content
Padding
Border
Margin
Example:
.box {
    width: 200px;
    height: 100px;

    padding: 20px;
    border: 2px solid black;
    margin: 30px;
}

3. Margin
Margin creates space outside an element.
.box {
    margin: 20px;
}
Individual sides
.box {
    margin-top: 10px;
    margin-right: 20px;
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    margin-left: 40px;
}
Shorthand
.box {
    margin: 10px 20px 30px 40px;
}
Order:
Top → Right → Bottom → Left
Center an element
.box {
    width: 500px;
    margin: 0 auto;
}
auto can be used to horizontally center a block element with a defined width.

4. Padding
Padding creates space inside an element, between the content and border.
.box {
    padding: 20px;
}
Example:
<div class="box">
    Hello World
</div>
.box {
    background-color: lightblue;
    padding: 30px;
}
Individual sides
.box {
    padding-top: 10px;
    padding-right: 20px;
    padding-bottom: 30px;
    padding-left: 40px;
}

5. Border
A border creates a visible boundary around an element.
.box {
    border: 2px solid black;
}
Border has three main properties:
border-width: 2px;
border-style: solid;
border-color: black;
Border styles
border-style: solid;
border-style: dashed;
border-style: dotted;
border-style: double;
Example:
.card {
    border: 1px solid gray;
    border-radius: 10px;
}
border-radius is used to create rounded corners.

